{"documentCount":6,"nextId":6,"documentIds":{"0":"Campaign Style.md","1":"Factions/Thieves Guild.md","2":"Locations/Old Harbor District.md","3":"Locations/Sea Spirits.md","4":"NPCs/Mira Shadowcloak.md","5":"_templates/npc.md"},"fieldIds":{"noteName":0,"content":1},"fieldLength":{"0":[2,83],"1":[2,77],"2":[3,91],"3":[2,102],"4":[2,76],"5":[1,64]},"averageFieldLength":[2,82.16666666666667],"storedFields":{"0":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/Campaign Style.md","noteName":"Campaign Style","content":"# Campaign Style — The Shattered Coast\n\n%% == LORECRAFT: CAMPAIGN STYLE == %%\n\n## Setting\nA dark, coastal fantasy world. City-states compete for trade routes.\nMagic is rare and distrusted by common folk.\n\n## Tone\nGritty and grounded. Think Joe Abercrombie, not Tolkien. Moral\nambiguity is expected. Heroes have flaws; villains have reasons.\n\n## Hard rules\n- No resurrection magic exists in this world\n- Gods are distant and do not intervene directly\n- Never invent a character's age — leave the Age field blank if unknown\n\n## Inspirations\n- The First Law trilogy (Joe Abercrombie)\n- Lies of Locke Lamora (Scott Lynch)\n"},"1":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/Factions/Thieves Guild.md","noteName":"Thieves Guild","content":"# Thieves Guild\n\n**Type:** Criminal faction\n**Base of operations:** [[Port Calderon]]\n**Leader:** [[Mira Shadowcloak]]\n**Status:** Active\n\n## Goals\nControl the black market trade routes through the Shattered Coast.\nMaintain plausible deniability with the city watch.\n\n## Allies\n- [[Harbor Master Voss]] — paid informant\n- [[The Pale Merchant]] — fence for stolen goods\n\n## Enemies\n- [[Inquisitors of the Coin]] — mercantile enforcement order\n- [[Dock Workers Union]] — competing for harbor control\n\n## Notes\nThe Guild does not tolerate killing civilians. It is a business, not\na war band. Members who draw unnecessary attention are dealt with\nquietly.\n"},"2":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/Locations/Old Harbor District.md","noteName":"Old Harbor District","content":"# Old Harbor District\n\n**Location:** [[Port Calderon]]\n**Status:** Contested\n\n## Overview\nThe oldest part of the city, where dockworkers load and unload cargo under the\nwatchful eye of [[Harbor Master Voss]]. The warehouses here change hands often.\n\n## Notable Features\n- The Tar & Tallow — a tavern where dockworkers drink after shift\n- Bonded Warehouse Row — long-term storage, controlled by the [[Thieves Guild]]\n- The Rat's Nest — a cramped tenement above a chandler's shop\n\n## Dangers\nSmugglers use the network of sea-caves beneath the district to move contraband.\nThe city watch patrols only the main thoroughfare; the back alleys belong to\nwhoever is boldest after dark.\n\n## Connections\n- [[Harbor Master Voss]] oversees legitimate trade\n- [[Thieves Guild]] taxes the smugglers through informal arrangement\n"},"3":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/Locations/Sea Spirits.md","noteName":"Sea Spirits","content":"# Sea Spirits\n\nAncient lore holds that the souls of drowned sailors linger near the wharves\nafter dark, drawn to the warmth of lanterns and the smell of tar. Fishermen\ncall them the Watchers — not dangerous, but unsettling. A candle left in a\nwindow is considered both an invitation and an appeasement.\n\n## Signs of Their Presence\n\nCold air that moves against the wind. Ropes that untie themselves overnight.\nThe sound of oars when no boat is visible. Experienced dockhands consider\nthese ordinary and pay them no mind; newcomers rarely sleep soundly in\ntheir first week near the water.\n\n## Offerings and Appeasement\n\nA small clay figurine cast into the water at the autumn equinox keeps the\nWatchers docile through winter. The tradition predates the city's founding;\nnobody knows who started it.\n"},"4":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/NPCs/Mira Shadowcloak.md","noteName":"Mira Shadowcloak","content":"# Mira Shadowcloak\n\n**Role:** Guild Master, [[Thieves Guild]]\n**Location:** [[Port Calderon]]\n**Age:**\n**Status:** Alive\n\n## Description\nA lean woman with close-cropped grey hair and the unhurried manner of\nsomeone who has never needed to raise her voice. She communicates\ndispleasure through silence.\n\n## Personality\nPragmatic to the point of coldness. Loyal to profit, not people.\nRespects competence above all else.\n\n## Secret\nShe was once an Inquisitor of the Coin. She knows their methods better\nthan they know themselves.\n\n## Connections\n- Leader of [[Thieves Guild]]\n- Old enemy: [[Commander Aldric]] (former colleague)\n"},"5":{"filePath":"/home/user/lorecraft/src/__tests__/fixtures/test-vault/_templates/npc.md","noteName":"npc","content":"# {{name}}\n\n%% == AGENT PROMPT ==\nGenerate a new NPC consistent with the campaign tone and the faction\nor location they belong to. Read the faction note and any linked NPCs\nbefore generating. The NPC should feel like they belong to the world\nalready described — not like a generic fantasy character.\n\n== INPUTS ==\n- name (required): The NPC's full name\n- faction (optional): Wikilink to the faction this NPC belongs to\n- location (optional): Wikilink to the NPC's base location\n- role (required): Brief description of their function in the campaign\n%%\n\n**Role:**\n**Location:**\n**Age:**\n**Status:** Alive\n\n## Description\n\n## Personality\n\n## Secret\n\n## Connections\n"}},"dirtCount":0,"index":[["know",{"1":{"4":1}}],["knows",{"1":{"3":1,"4":1}}],["keeps",{"1":{"3":1}}],["killing",{"1":{"1":1}}],["use",{"1":{"2":1}}],["unhurried",{"1":{"4":1}}],["untie",{"1":{"3":1}}],["unsettling",{"1":{"3":1}}],["under",{"1":{"2":1}}],["unload",{"1":{"2":1}}],["unnecessary",{"1":{"1":1}}],["union",{"1":{"1":1}}],["unknown",{"1":{"0":1}}],["quietly",{"1":{"1":1}}],["else",{"1":{"4":1}}],["equinox",{"1":{"3":1}}],["eye",{"1":{"2":1}}],["ene